title: 'Decided: one ''Hides nothing:'' line per child that left, naming the rule that held, not one bare "Hides nothing." per save.'
pid: 5a10b1a3-6f1a-45d3-a10e-35acc7c828ef
body: |2-
  Top asked for "Hides nothing." and for the rule where it costs little;
  the rule is the useful part, and naming the child says which removal
  failed when a save makes several. The rules, as the server finds them:
  the child is no content of any subscribee and overrides none of it
  (Top's "the subscriber's own" and "never the subscribee's content" are
  both this one); what it stands for was hidden already; the subscriber
  still contains what it stands for; the same save shows it in the
  subscribee folder. A removal from a note that subscribes to nothing, or
  of a node the save deletes, prints nothing.
